# 1640s (2026-10-18): farmer conscripts and clubmen - a rush when the enemy is close and few,
# gone for home when it goes badly.
drill "Clubmen"
era 1640s
about "Farmers with bills and flails: a howling rush when the enemy is close and not too many, gone for home when it goes badly."
type Clubman
dials aggression 0.70 discipline 0.20 cohesion 0.50 cover 0.40 patience 0.30 nerve 0.28

sergeant:
  when my losses over 30%                                -> fall back 40
  when horse charging                                    -> fall back 20
  when enemy breaking                                    -> charge
  when enemy within 30 and not enemy outnumbers us       -> charge
  otherwise                                              -> advance

man:
  otherwise                                              -> follow sergeant
